#. page title
msgctxt "before-you-start"
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#. page description
msgctxt "before-you-start"
msgid ""
"What to check in PrusaSlicer and on the printer before printing any "
"calibration test."
msgstr ""

#. page intro
msgctxt "before-you-start"
msgid ""
"Five minutes here save a wasted test. These checks are the same for every "
"test in the suite; each guide only adds what is special to it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "before-you-start/version"
msgid "PrusaSlicer version"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/version"
msgid ""
"Use **PrusaSlicer 2.9**. 2.7 and 2.8 also open the projects; older versions "
"load only the shape, without the changes that make it a test."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/version"
msgid ""
"PrusaSlicer 3.x is still alpha and these files are not tested with it yet."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/version"
msgid ""
"Always open tests with **File › Open project**, never with **Import**, and "
"download single .3mf files, never ZIPs."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "before-you-start/printer-ready"
msgid "A printer that already prints"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/printer-ready"
msgid ""
"The tests calibrate the fine details. They assume the basics are right: "
"tight belts, a level (or meshed) bed, a hotend without leaks, a working "
"part-cooling fan."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/printer-ready"
msgid ""
"Do the firmware checks first on a new printer: PID tuning of hotend and "
"bed, extruder steps (rotation distance), and input shaping if your printer "
"has it."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/printer-ready"
msgid ""
"The **first layer** test comes before all the others: every test stands on "
"its first layer."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "before-you-start/dry-filament"
msgid "Dry filament"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/dry-filament"
msgid ""
"If a spool has been out of its bag for weeks (days for PETG, TPU, nylon and "
"PC), dry it before calibrating."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "before-you-start/dry-filament"
msgid ""
"Wet filament strings, pops, and makes weak layers at **every** temperature. "
"It ruins the temperature, retraction and flow tests in ways that look like "
"wrong settings."
msgstr ""

#. More: point (beginner)
msgctxt "before-you-start/dry-filament"
msgid ""
"Crackling or small bubbles on the extruded plastic are the classic signs of "
"wet filament."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "before-you-start/profiles"
msgid "Your profiles, not ours"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/profiles"
msgid ""
"The tests carry no printer, filament or print profile. Before slicing, "
"select in PrusaSlicer **your** printer, the **print profile you really "
"use** and the **filament profile** of the spool you test."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/profiles"
msgid ""
"Save every result in a **new** filament profile with a clear name (brand, "
"type, colour, value). Keep the original."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "before-you-start/profiles"
msgid ""
"A test printed with a different speed or layer height from your real prints "
"gives an answer for a different situation."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "before-you-start/profiles"
msgid ""
"Some tests set a few per-object settings (layer height, perimeters, "
"infill). Leave them: they are part of the test."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "before-you-start/global-settings"
msgid "Global settings to check"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/global-settings"
msgid ""
"One test per plate. The per-layer changes belong to the plate, so opening a "
"test replaces what was there, and another object on the plate would receive "
"the same changes."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "before-you-start/global-settings"
msgid ""
"Do not scale, rotate, cut or sink a test object: its changes are at fixed "
"heights."
msgstr ""

