#. More: point
msgctxt "home/fast-or-full"
msgid ""
"**Firmware checks** are not printed tests: belts, PID tuning, extruder "
"steps (rotation distance) and input shaping are done with your firmware's "
"own tools. Do them before the first layer."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/fast-or-full"
msgid ""
"On an IDEX or multi-tool printer, calibrate each tool's filament on that "
"tool, or at least on the tool you will use."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid "Why this order"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid ""
"Follow the contents from top to bottom: each test builds on the ones before "
"it."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid "**First layer first:** every other test sits on it."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid ""
"**Temperature before everything else for a filament:** flow, pressure "
"advance and retraction all change with temperature."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid ""
"**Maximum volumetric flow before pressure advance:** pressure advance is "
"calibrated at speeds the hotend can really melt."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid ""
"**Pressure advance before flow:** the flow test reads top surfaces, which "
"pressure advance changes."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid ""
"**Retraction last:** good pressure advance often removes most stringing by "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "home/order"
msgid ""
"The tests not written yet are listed in grey: they arrive one at a time."
msgstr ""

#. page title
msgctxt "idex-alignment-scorecard"
msgid "IDEX alignment card"
msgstr ""

#. page description
msgctxt "idex-alignment-scorecard"
msgid ""
"Type the X and Y readings of each station: the card fits offset, scale and "
"skew, gives a verdict per mechanism and prints the firmware lines."
msgstr ""

#. page intro
msgctxt "idex-alignment-scorecard"
msgid ""
"Type the readings of each station, in mm, as explained in the [IDEX "
"alignment guide](page:idex-alignment#read-vernier). The card works out the "
"tool offset at the bed centre, a verdict for each mechanism, and the lines "
"to type into RatOS, PrusaSlicer, a Prusa XL or Marlin. Nothing is sent "
"anywhere: the calculation runs in your browser.\n"
"\n"
"Write down too: **printer**, **nozzles**, **filament**, **date**, and the "
"**offsets before the change**. The next run is compared with this one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. page breadcrumb
msgctxt "idex-alignment-scorecard"
msgid "Printable card"
msgstr ""

#. callout
msgctxt "idex-alignment-scorecard"
msgid ""
"Follows the IDEX alignment test v1.0.0 (Lite and Vernier), 0.4 mm nozzle, "
"bed presets as in the guide. Printed on A4: the rules on page 1, the grid "
"on page 2."
msgstr ""

#. page title
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid "IDEX / multi-tool alignment"
msgstr ""

#. page description
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid ""
"Check the XY offset between two toolheads at every spot of the bed, read it "
"to 0.05 mm, and find out whether a drift comes from the offset or from the "
"mechanics."
msgstr ""

#. page intro
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid ""
"One layer, two tools, a small station at every corner and edge of the bed. "
"At each station T1 prints next to T0, and you read how far apart they "
"landed, **in X and in Y**. The same gap everywhere is a plain offset; a gap "
"that changes across the bed is mechanical.\n"
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid ""
"If the gap is the same everywhere, one number fixes it. If it changes "
"across the bed, the cause is mechanical, and the pattern says where to look."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid ""
"There are two versions. **Lite** shows gap or overlap at a glance and uses "
"under 0.5 g of filament. **Vernier** reads numbers to **0.05 mm** and uses "
"under 2 g. Both print in minutes."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid ""
"The [interactive card](page:idex-alignment-scorecard) turns your readings "
"into the offset, a verdict for each mechanism and the lines to type into "
"your firmware."
msgstr ""

#. callout
msgctxt "idex-alignment"
msgid ""
"Open the file with **File › Open project**, never with **Import**. Set "
"**skirt loops to 0**, and keep the tool offsets in **one place only**: in "
"the firmware (RatOS) **or** in the slicer, never both ([step "
"3](page:idex-alignment#prepare))."
msgstr ""

