#. part heading (groups steps)
msgctxt "max-flow"
msgid "Print it"
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid "Open it as a project and check the preview"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**File › Open project** (Ctrl+O, ⌘O on macOS), pick your profiles, slice."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"Leave it as it opens: the **long side along X** (left to right). Every file "
"but `uhf-0.4` fits a 180 mm bed."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"In the Preview legend choose **Volumetric flow rate** and hover each band "
"on a long straight: it must show **the number on the column**."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid "The print time shown is the real one."
msgstr ""

#. photo alt
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"PrusaSlicer preview of the hf-0.4 flow test in Volumetric flow rate view: "
"colour bands up the wall, the legend from 0.74 to 42.5 mm³/s, the band 6 "
"marker on the slider showing flow=30 and M220 S1049"
msgstr ""

#. photo caption
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"Preview, Volumetric flow rate (hf-0.4): one colour per band up the wall; "
"the slider marker of band 6 reads flow=30."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"Dragging the file in? Choose **Open as project**, never **Import 3D models "
"only**."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**Volumetric flow rate** is the check that nothing in the slicer capped the "
"test: on the long straights band 1 shows the lowest number, the top of the "
"legend the highest (32.0 on standard-0.4). On the fast files the top of the "
"legend can stay below the top label (on the screenshot above, 42.5 instead "
"of 50 on hf-0.4): read each band's value from its marker on the slider "
"(`flow=…`), and make sure the printer itself allows the top speed "
"([firmware limits](page:max-flow#firmware-limits)). The numbers on the "
"column print at half speed and show lower values: that is intended. "
"**Speed** shows the band speeds (21–168 mm/s on standard-0.4). The layer "
"height is 0.75 × the nozzle (0.30 mm on the 0.4 files), whatever your "
"profile says."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**Feature type:** one **External perimeter** line per layer, and **nothing "
"inside the wedge**: no infill, no floor, no gap fill. The numbers face is a "
"small solid block on the column. The **seam** sits on the column's rear "
"corner on every layer, never on the long straights or the round end."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"The vertical slider shows one marker per band; hovering shows `M220 S…`. In "
"the G-code each band starts with `;CALIB max_flow band=N/M flow=X`, where M "
"is the file's number of bands (15 on standard-0.4, 11 on hf-0.4)."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**The print time is reliable** with Klipper, Marlin and Prusa printer "
"profiles: PrusaSlicer's preview and time estimate apply `M220`."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**RepRapFirmware printer profiles:** the preview ignores `M220`. The legend "
"shows the slow base speed (5–17 mm/s; 13.5 on standard-0.4) and the time is "
"several times too long; the printer still prints the real bands."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**All bands lower than the engraved numbers, by the same ratio?** Your "
"filament profile slowed the base speed down. For this slice only: in "
"**Filament Settings › Cooling** set **Slow down if layer print time is "
"below** and **Enable fan if layer print time is below** to 5 s, and/or "
"raise **Max volumetric speed** above 6.5 mm³/s; slice, export, then "
"**discard** the change (never save it)."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**Spiral vase** and **Sequential printing** must be off. Gap fill or infill "
"must not appear: if it does, the file was imported."
msgstr ""

#. More: point (expert)
msgctxt "max-flow/open-project"
msgid ""
"**Why along X.** On a bed slinger, X moves only the toolhead, the lighter "
"axis. On CoreXY either axis is fine; keep X so results compare."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid "No profile changes: how the speed rises"
msgstr ""

#. callout title
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid "If you cancel the print, send M220 S100"
msgstr ""

#. callout
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"The top of the tower sets the speed back with `M220 S100`. If you "
"**cancel** before the top, type **`M220 S100`** in the printer's console: "
"Klipper, Marlin and RepRapFirmware keep the factor, and your next print "
"would run up to 8–29 times too fast, up to the firmware's limits. Prusa "
"Buddy printers reset it at the next print start."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"**Leave your profiles as they are**, including the filament's max "
"volumetric speed: the slicer cannot cap what the printer adds."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"The file asks PrusaSlicer for one slow speed (13.5 mm/s on standard-0.4). "
"At the start of each band, `M220 S<percent>` tells the printer to run "
"everything that many times faster: `M220 S1010` is 10.1 ×."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"**Flow = speed × line area.** standard-0.4, band 26: 13.5 mm/s × 10.10 × "
"0.1907 mm² = 26.0 mm³/s."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"PrusaSlicer's cooling logic (*Slow down if layer print time is below*, "
"*Enable fan if below*) and the filament's max volumetric speed only see the "
"slow speed: they never slow the bands down, and the fan stays at your "
"filament's normal setting."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"`M220` works on Marlin, Prusa firmware (MK4/MK4S, MK3.9/3.5, Core One, XL, "
"MINI, MK3), Klipper and RepRapFirmware: one file for every printer."
msgstr ""

#. More: point
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"`M220` also speeds up travel and retraction moves. Your firmware limits cap "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. More: point (expert)
msgctxt "max-flow/how-it-works"
msgid ""
"The factors go up to about 2900 %. One unconfirmed report says factors of "
"1000 % or more misbehave on an unnamed printer; no firmware source we read "
"clamps them. If yours does, the bands above it stop getting faster and look "
"better than their label: generate a file with `--max-factor 999`."
msgstr ""

#. step title
msgctxt "max-flow/firmware-limits"
msgid "Check your firmware limits"
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/firmware-limits"
msgid ""
"**Klipper:** `max_velocity` in `[printer]` at least the top speed in the "
"table, `max_accel` at least the acceleration (or `SET_VELOCITY_LIMIT` for "
"this session)."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/firmware-limits"
msgid ""
"**Marlin:** `M203` X/Y at least the top speed and **`M203 E`** at least the "
"filament speed. **Prusa:** **Printer Settings › Machine limits**."
msgstr ""

#. point
msgctxt "max-flow/firmware-limits"
msgid ""
"Above a limit the speed stops rising: the band prints below its label and "
"looks better than it should."
msgstr ""

